        "text": "Genres: Simulation,Sports,Casual. Tags: Physics,Ball,Crafting,Sandbox. About: Step into a hands-on workshop devoted to the design, history, and practical use of balls. Choose materials, compare their strengths and properties, and build equivalent balls to see how construction changes their performance. Begin with classic forms, including traditional horned designs, or try a slim B-ball and the distinctive Baxter model. Each design has trade-offs: handmade assembly and familiar construction methods can offer useful qualities while bringing their own complications.\n\nCreate and compare a collection of up to 16 balls, then test them with a 250 W power-holder. Explore how regional traditions and real-world applications shape material choices, from everyday play to specialized uses. Study the features that made earlier designs popular, refine your own functional builds, and weigh each advantage against the demands of production. Experiment, test, and uncover how thoughtful design turns simple materials into objects made to move.",
