        "text": "Title: Triangle Closing for Recruiter Search on LinkedIn: Location-Aware Candidate Retrieval Across Cities and Metropolitan Areas. Abstract: Recruiters on LinkedIn search for candidates across many cities and metropolitan areas, yet location and job-title fields are noisy and inconsistent. We study recruiter search as link prediction on a heterogeneous graph of recruiters, candidates, jobs, companies, and locations, using triangles as the central structural signal. Our method scores a recruiter-candidate pair by counting closed triples through shared employers, industries, and areas. We normalize location strings and job-title variants and feed the triangle counts into a ranking model. On a large offline dataset of recruiter interactions, the approach improves ranking quality over text-only and embedding baselines, especially for rare titles and small areas. Ablations show that location-aware triangles account for most of the gain.",
