        "sha256": "2959579a0fb090f246314d5890b48f20d03ff3c5b64ff149b2842f363005aac2",
        "text": "Title: Triangles Conquer Recruiter via LI. Abstract: We study triangle-based candidate discovery for recruiters on LinkedIn (LI). Recruiters, candidates, and organizations form a heterogeneous graph, where a triangle represents mutually reinforcing connections among these entities. We score recruiter\u2013candidate links using local triangle patterns alongside profile and employment signals, then rank candidates for outreach. This approach favors candidates supported by multiple paths through the network while retaining useful evidence from sparse neighborhoods. Recommendations can be interpreted through the shared connections and organizational context contributing to each score. The source draft contains no recoverable dataset, benchmark, or quantitative findings; accordingly, this description makes no performance claims and frames the contribution as a graph-based method and evaluation protocol for recruiter\u2013candidate interactions.",
